# Main game = the game

## Non-negotiable truth

The **main-scene run** (today: `Assets/Scripts/MainGame/`, `MainGameController`) is **Terraforming Tendencies**—the same loop the shipped game will use: planet surface, sectors, survey-as-puzzle, typed resources, cards, placement, build weeks, End Week, corporate pressure.

**`MainGame*` types are the authoritative sim**; do not fork a parallel “real game” later without explicit direction.

## Do

- Extend **main-game systems** toward the full product: `MainGameController`, `MainGameColony`, shared planet (`PlanetGenerator`, `SectorManager`), cards, `ColonyTileGrid`, placement, HUD.
- Frame plans as **game-wide** (perf, DOTS, culling, fog, economy, UI)—applicable as the run grows (more sectors, planet pick), not “main-game-only” hacks.
- Treat **player verification** on the main run as verifying **the game** ([`player-verify-after-changes.mdc`](player-verify-after-changes.mdc)).
- Use **archived** only where the repo already says so (e.g. **Colony Acts**), not for the main run.

## Do not

- Call the main run a **separate module**, **tutorial**, **demo**, **one-off**, or **side quest**.
- Propose **main-game-only** code paths or optimizations that duplicate mechanics the full game will need.
- Split architecture into “main game” vs “real game” (e.g. two fog systems, two economies) without explicit user direction.

## How agents talk to the player (required)

**Use:** the **game**, **main game**, **main run**, **current run**, **main scene**.

**Do not frame work as** “prologue work” or a “prologue project” (legacy Unreal label only—do not revive in chat).

**Harness filenames** (`main-game-ui-playthrough.sh`, etc.) are historical renames; describe them as **game playtests**.